# Maze Linux (maze-hardening): members of group wheel may use sudo — with their
# own password.
#
# Named 00-* on purpose. sudo reads /etc/sudoers.d in lexical order and the LAST
# matching rule wins. On the live ISO the passwordless 10-maze rule sorts after
# this one and wins; the installer deletes 10-maze, and this rule is what every
# installed system is left with.
%wheel ALL=(ALL:ALL) ALL
